a null collection names its caller before it dies

CFDictionaryGetValue on a NULL dictionary segfaults inside CoreFoundation, exactly as it does on
macOS. This does not change that. It changes the crash from an address into a stack.

An application that reads a sub-dictionary out of a Core Foundation object and does not check the
result lands here, and the only clue is the KEY, which is a pointer into some framework's constant
data. That is how #212 was read: the key resolved to kCTFontWeightTrait, so the caller had asked
something for a font traits dictionary and been handed nothing.

With the backtrace it took one run instead:

  CoreFoundation CFDictionaryGetValue on a NULL collection, key 0x78af935e9180
  CoreFoundation   1  mmex  wxNativeFontInfo::GetCTWeight(__CTFont const*) + 51
  CoreFoundation   2  mmex  wxFontRefData::Alloc() + 2111
  CoreFoundation   3  mmex  wxFont::OSXGetCTFont() const + 40
  CoreFoundation   9  mmex  wxHtmlWinParser::CreateCurrentFont() + 626

__func__ rather than a literal name, because this file is compiled once for CFDictionary and once
for CFSet.

MEASURED ON THE ROSTER: zero NULL collection lookups across all five applications, so this surfaces
no latent defect in anything that already works.

--- a/CFDictionary.c
+++ b/CFDictionary.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include <CoreFoundation/CFDictionary.h>
 #include "CFInternal.h"
 #include "CFBasicHash.h"
+#include <execinfo.h>
 #include <CoreFoundation/CFString.h>
 
 
@@ -404,6 +405,25 @@
 }
 
 const_any_pointer_t CFDictionaryGetValue(CFHashRef hc, const_any_pointer_t key) {
+    /* A NULL COLLECTION NAMES ITS CALLER BEFORE IT DIES. macOS crashes here too, so this changes
+     * nothing about what happens; it changes the crash from an address in CoreFoundation into a
+     * stack. An application that reads a sub-dictionary out of a Core Foundation object and does
+     * not check the result lands here, and the only clue is the KEY.
+     *
+     * That is how #212 was read: the key was kCTFontWeightTrait, so the caller had asked something
+     * for a font traits dictionary and been given nothing. __func__ rather than a literal name
+     * because this file is compiled once for CFDictionary and once for CFSet. */
+    if (hc == NULL) {
+        void *frames[24];
+        int count = backtrace(frames, 24);
+        char **names = backtrace_symbols(frames, count);
+
+        fprintf(stderr, "CoreFoundation %s on a NULL collection, key %p\n", __func__, key);
+        for (int i = 1; i < count && names != NULL; i++)
+            fprintf(stderr, "CoreFoundation   %s\n", names[i]);
+        free(names);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
 #if CFDictionary
     if (CFDictionary) CF_OBJC_FUNCDISPATCHV(CFDictionaryGetTypeID(), const_any_pointer_t, (NSDictionary *)hc, objectForKey:(id)key);
 #endif
